<%# One episode card of a product page -- the customer page and the admin preview render the same card so the preview
    shows what a customer sees (handoff 0066). Only the link target differs, and the admin preview adds the episode's
    status after the number and says "편집하기 →" instead of "학습 시작 →", because its link opens the admin edit page.
    The "E" is display only: display_id is also the URL segment (digits only), so the model is untouched.
    The customer CTA is fixed text: there is no per-episode progress to vary it by.

    Handoff 0067 -- number, title and CTA sit on one row (number and CTA never shrink or wrap; only the title does,
    via truncate + a title tooltip, same as before). Below `sm` there usually isn't room for a fourth width (number +
    a readable title + CTA), so the CTA alone drops to its own line there (`w-full` forces the wrap; `sm:w-auto` plus
    `sm:ml-auto` puts it back at the right end of the row) -- number and title always stay together on the first
    line. No per-episode state (e.g. a lock icon) exists on this card today. %>
<% admin = local_assigns.fetch(:admin, false) %>
<% title = episode.customer_title.presence || "(제목 없음)" %>
<%= link_to path, class: "block rounded-xl border border-gray-200 p-4 hover:border-blue-300" do %>
  <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-3 gap-y-1">
    <span class="shrink-0 text-xs font-semibold text-gray-400">E<%= episode.display_id %><% if admin %> · <%= episode.status %><% end %></span>
    <span class="min-w-0 flex-1 truncate font-bold text-gray-900" title="<%= title %>"><%= title %></span>
    <span class="order-last w-full shrink-0 whitespace-nowrap text-sm font-semibold text-blue-600 sm:order-none sm:ml-auto sm:w-auto"><%= admin ? "편집하기 →" : "학습 시작 →" %></span>
  </div>
<% end %>
